---
id: isr
title: Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR) allows you to serve statically generated content from a CDN while periodically regenerating it in the background. This gives you the performance benefits of static sites with the freshness of dynamic content."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-isr-works-in-tanstack-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How ISR Works in TanStack Start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start's approach to ISR is flexible and leverages standard HTTP cache headers that work with any CDN. Unlike framework-specific ISR implementations, this approach gives you full control over caching behavior at both the page and data level."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The core concept is simple:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Prerendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Pages are generated at build time"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN Caching"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Cache headers control how long CDNs cache the HTML"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revalidation"}]},{"type":"text","value":": After the cache expires, the next request triggers regeneration"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stale-While-Revalidate"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Serve stale content while fetching fresh data in the background"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cache-header-strategies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache Header Strategies"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"time-based-revalidation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time-Based Revalidation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The most common ISR pattern uses the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Cache-Control"},{"type":"text","value":" header with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max-age"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s-maxage"},{"type":"text","value":" directives:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache at CDN for 1 hour, allow stale content for up to 1 day\n    'Cache-Control':\n      'public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n\nexport default function BlogPost() {\n  const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n      <div>{post.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"understanding-cache-control-directives","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Understanding Cache-Control Directives"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Response can be cached by any cache (CDN, browser, etc.)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"max-age=3600"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Content is fresh for 3600 seconds (1 hour)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"s-maxage=3600"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Overrides max-age for shared caches (CDNs)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stale-while-revalidate=86400"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Serve stale content while revalidating in background for up to 24 hours"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"immutable"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Content never changes (use for hash-based assets)"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"isr-with-server-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ISR with Server Functions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server functions can also set cache headers for dynamic data endpoints:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params, request }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n\n        return Response.json(\n          { product },\n          {\n            headers: {\n              'Cache-Control':\n                'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600',\n              'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=3600', // Cloudflare-specific\n            },\n          },\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"using-middleware-for-cache-headers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using Middleware for Cache Headers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For API routes, you can use middleware to set cache headers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst cacheMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Add cache headers to the response\n  result.response.headers.set(\n    'Cache-Control',\n    'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  )\n\n  return result\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    middleware: [cacheMiddleware],\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n        return Response.json({ product })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For page routes, it's simpler to use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers"},{"type":"text","value":" property directly:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"on-demand-revalidation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On-Demand Revalidation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"While time-based revalidation works well for most cases, you may need to invalidate specific pages immediately (e.g., when content is updated):"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/revalidate.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/revalidate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const { path, secret } = await request.json()\n\n        // Verify secret token\n        if (secret !== process.env.REVALIDATE_SECRET) {\n          return Response.json({ error: 'Invalid token' }, { status: 401 })\n        }\n\n        // Trigger CDN purge via your CDN's API\n        await fetch(\n          `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/${ZONE_ID}/purge_cache`,\n          {\n            method: 'POST',\n            headers: {\n              Authorization: `Bearer ${CF_API_TOKEN}`,\n              'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n            },\n            body: JSON.stringify({\n              files: [`https://yoursite.com${path}`],\n            }),\n          },\n        )\n\n        return Response.json({ revalidated: true })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cdn-specific-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN-Specific Configuration"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cloudflare-workers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare Workers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare respects standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Cache-Control"},{"type":"text","value":" headers and provides additional control:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600',\n    // Cloudflare-specific header for finer control\n    'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=7200',\n  }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"netlify","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Netlify"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Netlify uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Cache-Control"},{"type":"text","value":" headers and also supports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_headers"},{"type":"text","value":" files:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# public/_headers\n/blog/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n\n/api/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300","lang":"plaintext"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"vercel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vercel"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When deploying to Vercel, use their Edge Network cache headers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"combining-isr-with-client-side-caching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combining ISR with Client-Side Caching"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router's built-in cache control works alongside CDN caching:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // CDN caching (via headers)\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n  // Client-side caching (via TanStack Router)\n  staleTime: 60_000, // Consider data fresh for 60 seconds on client\n  gcTime: 5 * 60_000, // Keep in memory for 5 minutes\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This creates a multi-tier caching strategy:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CDN Edge"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 1 hour cache, stale-while-revalidate for 24 hours"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client"}]},{"type":"text","value":": 60 seconds of fresh data, 5 minutes in memory"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-isr-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common ISR Patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"blog-posts","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Blog Posts"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/$slug')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchPost(params.slug),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache for 1 hour, allow stale for 7 days\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 5 * 60_000, // 5 minutes client-side\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"e-commerce-product-pages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"E-commerce Product Pages"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchProduct(params.id),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Shorter cache due to inventory changes\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000, // 30 seconds client-side\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"marketing-landing-pages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Marketing Landing Pages"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/landing/$campaign')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchCampaign(params.campaign),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Long cache for stable content\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 60 * 60_000, // 1 hour client-side\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"user-specific-pages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"User-Specific Pages"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => fetchUserData(),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Private cache, no CDN caching\n    'Cache-Control': 'private, max-age=60',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"best-practices","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best Practices"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"1-start-conservative","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Start Conservative"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Begin with shorter cache times and increase as you understand your content update patterns:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Start here\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600'\n\n// Then move to\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"2-use-etags-for-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Use ETags for Validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ETags help CDNs efficiently revalidate content:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport crypto from 'crypto'\n\nconst etagMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Generate ETag from response content\n  const etag = crypto\n    .createHash('md5')\n    .update(JSON.stringify(result.data))\n    .digest('hex')\n\n  result.response.headers.set('ETag', `\"${etag}\"`)\n\n  return result\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"3-vary-cache-by-query-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Vary Cache by Query Parameters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When content varies by query params, include them in cache keys:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300',\n    Vary: 'Accept, Accept-Encoding',\n  }),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"4-monitor-cache-hit-rates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Monitor Cache Hit Rates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Track CDN performance to optimize cache times:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const cacheMonitoringMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const result = await next()\n\n    // Log cache status (from CDN headers)\n    console.log('Cache Status:', result.response.headers.get('cf-cache-status'))\n\n    return result\n  },\n)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"5-combine-with-static-prerendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Combine with Static Prerendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prerender at build time for instant first load, then use ISR for updates:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"bundler"},"children":[{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"vite","data-tab-index":"0","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"vite.config.ts\"","title":"vite.config.ts","file":"vite.config.ts"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tab-panel","tagName":"md-tab-panel","attributes":{},"properties":{"data-tab-slug":"rsbuild","data-tab-index":"1","data-content":"code-only"},"children":[{"type":"code","value":"import { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts","meta":"title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"","title":"rsbuild.config.ts","file":"rsbuild.config.ts"}]}],"properties":{"data-attributes":"{\"tabs\":[{\"slug\":\"vite\",\"name\":\"vite\"},{\"slug\":\"rsbuild\",\"name\":\"rsbuild\"}]}","data-bundler-meta":"{\"bundlers\":[\"vite\",\"rsbuild\"]}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"debugging-isr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging ISR"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"check-cache-headers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check Cache Headers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use browser DevTools or curl to inspect cache headers:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"curl -I https://yoursite.com/blog/my-post\n\n# Look for:\n# Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n# Age: 1234 (time in cache)\n# X-Cache: HIT (from CDN)","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"test-revalidation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Test Revalidation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Force cache misses to test regeneration:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"# Cloudflare: Bypass cache\ncurl -H \"Cache-Control: no-cache\" https://yoursite.com/page\n\n# Or use CDN-specific cache purge APIs","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"monitor-performance","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monitor Performance"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Track key metrics:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cache Hit Rate"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Percentage of requests served from cache"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Revalidation Time"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Time to regenerate stale content"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time to First Byte (TTFB)"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Should be low for cached content"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related-resources","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related Resources"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./static-prerendering.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Static Prerendering"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Build-time page generation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./hosting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosting"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - CDN deployment configurations"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./server-functions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Functions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Creating dynamic data endpoints"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/router/latest/docs/guide/data-loading","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Loading"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Client-side cache control"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Request/response customization"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"how-isr-works-in-tanstack-start","text":"How ISR Works in TanStack Start","level":2},{"id":"cache-header-strategies","text":"Cache Header Strategies","level":2},{"id":"time-based-revalidation","text":"Time-Based Revalidation","level":3},{"id":"understanding-cache-control-directives","text":"Understanding Cache-Control Directives","level":3},{"id":"isr-with-server-functions","text":"ISR with Server Functions","level":2},{"id":"using-middleware-for-cache-headers","text":"Using Middleware for Cache Headers","level":3},{"id":"on-demand-revalidation","text":"On-Demand Revalidation","level":2},{"id":"cdn-specific-configuration","text":"CDN-Specific Configuration","level":2},{"id":"cloudflare-workers","text":"Cloudflare Workers","level":3},{"id":"netlify","text":"Netlify","level":3},{"id":"vercel","text":"Vercel","level":3},{"id":"combining-isr-with-client-side-caching","text":"Combining ISR with Client-Side Caching","level":2},{"id":"common-isr-patterns","text":"Common ISR Patterns","level":2},{"id":"blog-posts","text":"Blog Posts","level":3},{"id":"e-commerce-product-pages","text":"E-commerce Product Pages","level":3},{"id":"marketing-landing-pages","text":"Marketing Landing Pages","level":3},{"id":"user-specific-pages","text":"User-Specific Pages","level":3},{"id":"best-practices","text":"Best Practices","level":2},{"id":"1-start-conservative","text":"1. Start Conservative","level":3},{"id":"2-use-etags-for-validation","text":"2. Use ETags for Validation","level":3},{"id":"3-vary-cache-by-query-parameters","text":"3. Vary Cache by Query Parameters","level":3},{"id":"4-monitor-cache-hit-rates","text":"4. Monitor Cache Hit Rates","level":3},{"id":"5-combine-with-static-prerendering","text":"5. Combine with Static Prerendering","level":3},{"id":"debugging-isr","text":"Debugging ISR","level":2},{"id":"check-cache-headers","text":"Check Cache Headers","level":3},{"id":"test-revalidation","text":"Test Revalidation","level":3},{"id":"monitor-performance","text":"Monitor Performance","level":3},{"id":"related-resources","text":"Related Resources","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nIncremental Static Regeneration (ISR) allows you to serve statically generated content from a CDN while periodically regenerating it in the background. This gives you the performance benefits of static sites with the freshness of dynamic content.\n\n## How ISR Works in TanStack Start\n\nTanStack Start's approach to ISR is flexible and leverages standard HTTP cache headers that work with any CDN. Unlike framework-specific ISR implementations, this approach gives you full control over caching behavior at both the page and data level.\n\nThe core concept is simple:\n\n1. **Static Prerendering**: Pages are generated at build time\n2. **CDN Caching**: Cache headers control how long CDNs cache the HTML\n3. **Revalidation**: After the cache expires, the next request triggers regeneration\n4. **Stale-While-Revalidate**: Serve stale content while fetching fresh data in the background\n\n## Cache Header Strategies\n\n### Time-Based Revalidation\n\nThe most common ISR pattern uses the `Cache-Control` header with `max-age` and `s-maxage` directives:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```tsx\n// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache at CDN for 1 hour, allow stale content for up to 1 day\n    'Cache-Control':\n      'public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n\nexport default function BlogPost() {\n  const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n      <div>{post.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Understanding Cache-Control Directives\n\n- **`public`**: Response can be cached by any cache (CDN, browser, etc.)\n- **`max-age=3600`**: Content is fresh for 3600 seconds (1 hour)\n- **`s-maxage=3600`**: Overrides max-age for shared caches (CDNs)\n- **`stale-while-revalidate=86400`**: Serve stale content while revalidating in background for up to 24 hours\n- **`immutable`**: Content never changes (use for hash-based assets)\n\n## ISR with Server Functions\n\nServer functions can also set cache headers for dynamic data endpoints:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params, request }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n\n        return Response.json(\n          { product },\n          {\n            headers: {\n              'Cache-Control':\n                'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600',\n              'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=3600', // Cloudflare-specific\n            },\n          },\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Using Middleware for Cache Headers\n\nFor API routes, you can use middleware to set cache headers:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst cacheMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Add cache headers to the response\n  result.response.headers.set(\n    'Cache-Control',\n    'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  )\n\n  return result\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    middleware: [cacheMiddleware],\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n        return Response.json({ product })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor page routes, it's simpler to use the `headers` property directly:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## On-Demand Revalidation\n\nWhile time-based revalidation works well for most cases, you may need to invalidate specific pages immediately (e.g., when content is updated):\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/revalidate.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/revalidate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const { path, secret } = await request.json()\n\n        // Verify secret token\n        if (secret !== process.env.REVALIDATE_SECRET) {\n          return Response.json({ error: 'Invalid token' }, { status: 401 })\n        }\n\n        // Trigger CDN purge via your CDN's API\n        await fetch(\n          `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/${ZONE_ID}/purge_cache`,\n          {\n            method: 'POST',\n            headers: {\n              Authorization: `Bearer ${CF_API_TOKEN}`,\n              'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n            },\n            body: JSON.stringify({\n              files: [`https://yoursite.com${path}`],\n            }),\n          },\n        )\n\n        return Response.json({ revalidated: true })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## CDN-Specific Configuration\n\n### Cloudflare Workers\n\nCloudflare respects standard `Cache-Control` headers and provides additional control:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600',\n    // Cloudflare-specific header for finer control\n    'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=7200',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### Netlify\n\nNetlify uses `Cache-Control` headers and also supports `_headers` files:\n\n```plaintext\n# public/_headers\n/blog/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n\n/api/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300\n```\n\n### Vercel\n\nWhen deploying to Vercel, use their Edge Network cache headers:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## Combining ISR with Client-Side Caching\n\nTanStack Router's built-in cache control works alongside CDN caching:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // CDN caching (via headers)\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n  // Client-side caching (via TanStack Router)\n  staleTime: 60_000, // Consider data fresh for 60 seconds on client\n  gcTime: 5 * 60_000, // Keep in memory for 5 minutes\n})\n```\n\nThis creates a multi-tier caching strategy:\n\n1. **CDN Edge**: 1 hour cache, stale-while-revalidate for 24 hours\n2. **Client**: 60 seconds of fresh data, 5 minutes in memory\n\n## Common ISR Patterns\n\n### Blog Posts\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/$slug')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchPost(params.slug),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache for 1 hour, allow stale for 7 days\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 5 * 60_000, // 5 minutes client-side\n})\n```\n\n### E-commerce Product Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchProduct(params.id),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Shorter cache due to inventory changes\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000, // 30 seconds client-side\n})\n```\n\n### Marketing Landing Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/landing/$campaign')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchCampaign(params.campaign),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Long cache for stable content\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 60 * 60_000, // 1 hour client-side\n})\n```\n\n### User-Specific Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => fetchUserData(),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Private cache, no CDN caching\n    'Cache-Control': 'private, max-age=60',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000,\n})\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Start Conservative\n\nBegin with shorter cache times and increase as you understand your content update patterns:\n\n```tsx\n// Start here\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600'\n\n// Then move to\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400'\n```\n\n### 2. Use ETags for Validation\n\nETags help CDNs efficiently revalidate content:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport crypto from 'crypto'\n\nconst etagMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Generate ETag from response content\n  const etag = crypto\n    .createHash('md5')\n    .update(JSON.stringify(result.data))\n    .digest('hex')\n\n  result.response.headers.set('ETag', `\"${etag}\"`)\n\n  return result\n})\n```\n\n### 3. Vary Cache by Query Parameters\n\nWhen content varies by query params, include them in cache keys:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300',\n    Vary: 'Accept, Accept-Encoding',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### 4. Monitor Cache Hit Rates\n\nTrack CDN performance to optimize cache times:\n\n```tsx\nconst cacheMonitoringMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const result = await next()\n\n    // Log cache status (from CDN headers)\n    console.log('Cache Status:', result.response.headers.get('cf-cache-status'))\n\n    return result\n  },\n)\n```\n\n### 5. Combine with Static Prerendering\n\nPrerender at build time for instant first load, then use ISR for updates:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Debugging ISR\n\n### Check Cache Headers\n\nUse browser DevTools or curl to inspect cache headers:\n\n```bash\ncurl -I https://yoursite.com/blog/my-post\n\n# Look for:\n# Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n# Age: 1234 (time in cache)\n# X-Cache: HIT (from CDN)\n```\n\n### Test Revalidation\n\nForce cache misses to test regeneration:\n\n```bash\n# Cloudflare: Bypass cache\ncurl -H \"Cache-Control: no-cache\" https://yoursite.com/page\n\n# Or use CDN-specific cache purge APIs\n```\n\n### Monitor Performance\n\nTrack key metrics:\n\n- **Cache Hit Rate**: Percentage of requests served from cache\n- **Revalidation Time**: Time to regenerate stale content\n- **Time to First Byte (TTFB)**: Should be low for cached content\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Static Prerendering](./static-prerendering.md) - Build-time page generation\n- [Hosting](./hosting.md) - CDN deployment configurations\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Creating dynamic data endpoints\n- [Data Loading](/router/latest/docs/guide/data-loading) - Client-side cache control\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) - Request/response customization\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: isr\ntitle: Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)\n---\n\nIncremental Static Regeneration (ISR) allows you to serve statically generated content from a CDN while periodically regenerating it in the background. This gives you the performance benefits of static sites with the freshness of dynamic content.\n\n## How ISR Works in TanStack Start\n\nTanStack Start's approach to ISR is flexible and leverages standard HTTP cache headers that work with any CDN. Unlike framework-specific ISR implementations, this approach gives you full control over caching behavior at both the page and data level.\n\nThe core concept is simple:\n\n1. **Static Prerendering**: Pages are generated at build time\n2. **CDN Caching**: Cache headers control how long CDNs cache the HTML\n3. **Revalidation**: After the cache expires, the next request triggers regeneration\n4. **Stale-While-Revalidate**: Serve stale content while fetching fresh data in the background\n\n## Cache Header Strategies\n\n### Time-Based Revalidation\n\nThe most common ISR pattern uses the `Cache-Control` header with `max-age` and `s-maxage` directives:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```tsx\n// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache at CDN for 1 hour, allow stale content for up to 1 day\n    'Cache-Control':\n      'public, max-age=3600, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n\nexport default function BlogPost() {\n  const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n  return (\n    <article>\n      <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n      <div>{post.content}</div>\n    </article>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n### Understanding Cache-Control Directives\n\n- **`public`**: Response can be cached by any cache (CDN, browser, etc.)\n- **`max-age=3600`**: Content is fresh for 3600 seconds (1 hour)\n- **`s-maxage=3600`**: Overrides max-age for shared caches (CDNs)\n- **`stale-while-revalidate=86400`**: Serve stale content while revalidating in background for up to 24 hours\n- **`immutable`**: Content never changes (use for hash-based assets)\n\n## ISR with Server Functions\n\nServer functions can also set cache headers for dynamic data endpoints:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params, request }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n\n        return Response.json(\n          { product },\n          {\n            headers: {\n              'Cache-Control':\n                'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600',\n              'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=3600', // Cloudflare-specific\n            },\n          },\n        )\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Using Middleware for Cache Headers\n\nFor API routes, you can use middleware to set cache headers:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/products/$productId.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\n\nconst cacheMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Add cache headers to the response\n  result.response.headers.set(\n    'Cache-Control',\n    'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  )\n\n  return result\n})\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/products/$productId')({\n  server: {\n    middleware: [cacheMiddleware],\n    handlers: {\n      GET: async ({ params }) => {\n        const product = await db.products.findById(params.productId)\n        return Response.json({ product })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nFor page routes, it's simpler to use the `headers` property directly:\n\n```tsx\n// routes/blog/posts/$postId.tsx\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    const post = await fetchPost(params.postId)\n    return { post }\n  },\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## On-Demand Revalidation\n\nWhile time-based revalidation works well for most cases, you may need to invalidate specific pages immediately (e.g., when content is updated):\n\n```tsx\n// routes/api/revalidate.ts\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/revalidate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const { path, secret } = await request.json()\n\n        // Verify secret token\n        if (secret !== process.env.REVALIDATE_SECRET) {\n          return Response.json({ error: 'Invalid token' }, { status: 401 })\n        }\n\n        // Trigger CDN purge via your CDN's API\n        await fetch(\n          `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/zones/${ZONE_ID}/purge_cache`,\n          {\n            method: 'POST',\n            headers: {\n              Authorization: `Bearer ${CF_API_TOKEN}`,\n              'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n            },\n            body: JSON.stringify({\n              files: [`https://yoursite.com${path}`],\n            }),\n          },\n        )\n\n        return Response.json({ revalidated: true })\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## CDN-Specific Configuration\n\n### Cloudflare Workers\n\nCloudflare respects standard `Cache-Control` headers and provides additional control:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600',\n    // Cloudflare-specific header for finer control\n    'CDN-Cache-Control': 'max-age=7200',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### Netlify\n\nNetlify uses `Cache-Control` headers and also supports `_headers` files:\n\n```plaintext\n# public/_headers\n/blog/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n\n/api/*\n  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300\n```\n\n### Vercel\n\nWhen deploying to Vercel, use their Edge Network cache headers:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$id')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n## Combining ISR with Client-Side Caching\n\nTanStack Router's built-in cache control works alongside CDN caching:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => {\n    return fetchPost(params.postId)\n  },\n  // CDN caching (via headers)\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400',\n  }),\n  // Client-side caching (via TanStack Router)\n  staleTime: 60_000, // Consider data fresh for 60 seconds on client\n  gcTime: 5 * 60_000, // Keep in memory for 5 minutes\n})\n```\n\nThis creates a multi-tier caching strategy:\n\n1. **CDN Edge**: 1 hour cache, stale-while-revalidate for 24 hours\n2. **Client**: 60 seconds of fresh data, 5 minutes in memory\n\n## Common ISR Patterns\n\n### Blog Posts\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/blog/$slug')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchPost(params.slug),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Cache for 1 hour, allow stale for 7 days\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 5 * 60_000, // 5 minutes client-side\n})\n```\n\n### E-commerce Product Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/products/$id')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchProduct(params.id),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Shorter cache due to inventory changes\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=3600',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000, // 30 seconds client-side\n})\n```\n\n### Marketing Landing Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/landing/$campaign')({\n  loader: async ({ params }) => fetchCampaign(params.campaign),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Long cache for stable content\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 60 * 60_000, // 1 hour client-side\n})\n```\n\n### User-Specific Pages\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/dashboard')({\n  loader: async () => fetchUserData(),\n  headers: () => ({\n    // Private cache, no CDN caching\n    'Cache-Control': 'private, max-age=60',\n  }),\n  staleTime: 30_000,\n})\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Start Conservative\n\nBegin with shorter cache times and increase as you understand your content update patterns:\n\n```tsx\n// Start here\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=600'\n\n// Then move to\n'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400'\n```\n\n### 2. Use ETags for Validation\n\nETags help CDNs efficiently revalidate content:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createMiddleware } from '@tanstack/react-start'\nimport crypto from 'crypto'\n\nconst etagMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(async ({ next }) => {\n  const result = await next()\n\n  // Generate ETag from response content\n  const etag = crypto\n    .createHash('md5')\n    .update(JSON.stringify(result.data))\n    .digest('hex')\n\n  result.response.headers.set('ETag', `\"${etag}\"`)\n\n  return result\n})\n```\n\n### 3. Vary Cache by Query Parameters\n\nWhen content varies by query params, include them in cache keys:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/search')({\n  headers: () => ({\n    'Cache-Control': 'public, max-age=300',\n    Vary: 'Accept, Accept-Encoding',\n  }),\n})\n```\n\n### 4. Monitor Cache Hit Rates\n\nTrack CDN performance to optimize cache times:\n\n```tsx\nconst cacheMonitoringMiddleware = createMiddleware().server(\n  async ({ next }) => {\n    const result = await next()\n\n    // Log cache status (from CDN headers)\n    console.log('Cache Status:', result.response.headers.get('cf-cache-status'))\n\n    return result\n  },\n)\n```\n\n### 5. Combine with Static Prerendering\n\nPrerender at build time for instant first load, then use ISR for updates:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"bundler\" -->\n\n# Vite\n\n```ts title=\"vite.config.ts\"\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/vite'\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n# Rsbuild\n\n```ts title=\"rsbuild.config.ts\"\nimport { defineConfig } from '@rsbuild/core'\nimport { pluginReact } from '@rsbuild/plugin-react'\nimport { tanstackStart } from '@tanstack/react-start/plugin/rsbuild'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [\n    pluginReact(),\n    tanstackStart({\n      prerender: {\n        routes: ['/blog', '/blog/posts/*'],\n        crawlLinks: true,\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## Debugging ISR\n\n### Check Cache Headers\n\nUse browser DevTools or curl to inspect cache headers:\n\n```bash\ncurl -I https://yoursite.com/blog/my-post\n\n# Look for:\n# Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400\n# Age: 1234 (time in cache)\n# X-Cache: HIT (from CDN)\n```\n\n### Test Revalidation\n\nForce cache misses to test regeneration:\n\n```bash\n# Cloudflare: Bypass cache\ncurl -H \"Cache-Control: no-cache\" https://yoursite.com/page\n\n# Or use CDN-specific cache purge APIs\n```\n\n### Monitor Performance\n\nTrack key metrics:\n\n- **Cache Hit Rate**: Percentage of requests served from cache\n- **Revalidation Time**: Time to regenerate stale content\n- **Time to First Byte (TTFB)**: Should be low for cached content\n\n## Related Resources\n\n- [Static Prerendering](./static-prerendering.md) - Build-time page generation\n- [Hosting](./hosting.md) - CDN deployment configurations\n- [Server Functions](./server-functions.md) - Creating dynamic data endpoints\n- [Data Loading](/router/latest/docs/guide/data-loading) - Client-side cache control\n- [Middleware](./middleware.md) - Request/response customization\n"}
